1
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:08,390
♪Don't stay trapped inside your room♪

2
00:00:08,390 --> 00:00:09,790
♪Outside the window,
the rain has cleared♪

3
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:11,070
♪Set reality aside♪

4
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:12,390
♪Follow your heart♪

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:13,750
♪What you've been longing
for is right ahead♪

6
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:15,230
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

7
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:18,110
♪Just be a little braver♪

8
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:20,870
♪Come closer, come closer♪

9
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:23,950
♪There's a little spark
shining in your eyes♪

10
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:26,070
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

11
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:29,790
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

12
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:33,820
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=
(Bonus Edition)

13
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:45,860
(Making breakfast)

14
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:51,960
Hi.

15
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:54,320
You made breakfast?

16
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:55,840
Yeah.

17
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:57,000
What are you making?

18
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:57,800
Almost done.

19
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,860
(Making breakfast together)

20
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:19,820
(Glances)

21
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:31,700
(Pay attention)

22
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:32,720
(Helping)

23
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:33,760
Just squeeze it onto my hand.

24
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:36,320
Thanks.

25
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:38,040
Did you put this on yourself?

26
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:39,960
You could say that.

27
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,640
Okay.

28
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:51,260
(Cooking meat patties)

29
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,440
Let's check the bread.

30
00:01:54,620 --> 00:01:55,200
(Glances)

31
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:56,240
See if it's done.

32
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:01,240
Is the bread done?

33
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,640
Why is it green?

34
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:05,520
Matcha.

35
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:06,920
Did you add matcha?

36
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:10,880
Is that matcha bread?

37
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:11,680
Yeah.

38
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:16,760
Do you think this one is spicy?

39
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:17,280
Which one?

40
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:17,720
This one.

41
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:18,240
This isn't spicy.

42
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,640
Then I'll add a little more to yours.

43
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:20,440
Okay.

44
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:25,980
(Breakfast is ready)

45
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:27,800
Where do you want to sit?

46
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,960
At the breakfast table?

47
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:31,320
Okay.

48
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:36,460
(A sunny breakfast table)

49
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,480
That looks pretty nice.

50
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:42,040
When can Xing

51
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:43,120
go out for a walk?

52
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:46,040
Probably pretty soon?

53
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,680
I'll check on her today.

54
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,120
She couldn't

55
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,800
go outside yesterday.

56
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:54,640
I don't know
if she's doing any better today.

57
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:55,420
(Glances)

58
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:56,800
Why do you always only eat half?

59
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:00,160
I'll take a break.

60
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,000
What's wrong?

61
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,160
Nothing.

62
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:10,160
We're kind of holding back, aren't we?

63
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:12,160
Not really.

64
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:16,980
(Glances)

65
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:20,940
(Asking for help)

66
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,040
Thanks.

67
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:27,120
Here.

68
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:35,080
Do you only eat cake

69
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,240
on your birthday?

70
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:39,120
I don't think
I even buy one for my birthday.

71
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,760
But my sister would make one.

72
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:42,240
For you?

73
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,480
That's impressive.

74
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:46,080
Whenever it's one of our birthdays,

75
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,360
she makes a little cake.

76
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,160
It's basically become a tradition.

77
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:52,320
Not really a tradition.

78
00:03:52,320 --> 00:03:53,080
A family tradition.

79
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:53,640
Yeah.

80
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:55,000
I guess it's just a habit.

81
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:57,520
My sister is really thoughtful.

82
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,760
She always thinks about all of us.

83
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,200
You guys must all be like that.

84
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,520
It's definitely mutual.

85
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:03,960
Yeah.

86
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,480
We usually

87
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:07,080
video call every day.

88
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,520
If we don't see each other for two days,

89
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,040
it feels kind of strange.

90
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:12,880
Then give them a video call

91
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:14,320
(Joking)
when you go out later.

92
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,560
(Shy)
Maybe I won't call them.

93
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,080
Why do you two

94
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:26,040
sound so cute

95
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:27,640
when you talk?

96
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:29,120
Is it because of your family?

97
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:29,560
The way you talk

98
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:30,680
is just so soft.

99
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:32,580
(Amused)

100
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,400
Aren't you like that too?

101
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:37,320
I'm almost turning into that.

102
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:38,720
I was kind of like that before.

103
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,920
I'm rubbing off on you.

104
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:42,680
Yeah, maybe I'm just not
as obvious as you.

105
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:43,480
Yeah.

106
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:44,840
Then I'll change it.

107
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:46,160
No, it's cute.

108
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,080
Why would you change it?

109
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:48,200
It's pretty good as it is.

110
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:52,960
I'll make you another dish
for dinner tonight.

111
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:55,040
If you don't see the extra dish,

112
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,280
that means I failed.

113
00:04:56,790 --> 00:04:58,200
(Encouraging him)
I'll definitely see it.

114
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:06,920
We'll go once we're done eating.

115
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:07,720
Sure.

116
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:10,720
Let's go.

117
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:29,880
You look really cute.

118
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:31,680
This one... It's a waste.

119
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,000
I'll draw a picture for it.

120
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:33,800
Sure.

121
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:37,920
Do you want to join me?

122
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,400
(Inviting)
I actually brought a bunch of these.

123
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:39,760
Wait a second.

124
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:40,520
Okay.

125
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:41,400
Just a moment.

126
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:54,180
(Hands over)

127
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,880
I wasn't really supposed
to show you this,

128
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:01,240
but I wanted to have some fun with you.

129
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,040
Let me think of something to draw.

130
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:04,640
Let's draw one together.

131
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:05,640
Let's draw something.

132
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:07,040
How about this butterfly?

133
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:07,880
You draw the other one.

134
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:09,400
How about you draw the other one?

135
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:10,560
Okay.

136
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:13,040
But I don't think I can draw like this.

137
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:13,560
What do you mean?

138
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:14,760
I'm not very good at this.

139
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:16,520
Give it a try.

140
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:21,000
Is that dizi yours?

141
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:21,560
Yeah.

142
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:22,240
Yu Yang.

143
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:22,920
Yeah.

144
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:27,240
I'll sit here.

145
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:32,640
You can even draw on wasted film?

146
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:33,440
Yeah.

147
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:34,240
What's this?

148
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:39,840
Can I...

149
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:40,540
Can I join you?

150
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:40,980
(Joining)

151
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:41,600
Here's a sheet for you.

152
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:42,640
Let's draw together.

153
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,880
Sounds good.

154
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:46,160
Come on.

155
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:50,040
I want some chalk.

156
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:52,600
This one. Okay.

157
00:06:57,200 --> 00:06:58,940
Mine doesn't look like a butterfly.

158
00:06:58,940 --> 00:06:59,560
What does it look like?

159
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:00,560
It looks good.

160
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:03,200
(Glances)
It looks like a moth.

161
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:09,220
(Teasing)
My butterfly isn't as pretty as yours.

162
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,240
Let me see.

163
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:11,680
I'll save it for you.

164
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:13,720
Yours looks really good.

165
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:14,760
It's good.

166
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:17,280
You could make that white outline
a little thicker.

167
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:17,720
Okay.

168
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:18,520
I think you can draw it.

169
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:19,800
Alright.

170
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:21,440
Okay.

171
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:23,400
Then let me fix the butterfly for you.

172
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:24,510
(Coaxing)
Study hard. Learn how to color.

173
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,440
Start learning now.

174
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,280
Start learning.

175
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:32,880
Feeling the pressure again.

176
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:36,960
(Praising)
Why does yours look so much better?

177
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:37,800
I...

178
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:40,160
I haven't even started.

179
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:43,280
It looks so natural.

180
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:44,380
(Keep praising)

181
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:46,640
It looks like
it's about to come to life.

182
00:07:58,880 --> 00:07:59,880
Let's look at the photo.

183
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,460
It looks good.

184
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,000
Okay.

185
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:11,680
If it doesn't look good,
you're in trouble.

186
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:14,880
Is this it, Mr. Cao?

187
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:16,560
No, it'll change.

188
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:17,940
But I think it looks good like this.

189
00:08:17,940 --> 00:08:19,020
(Comes closer)

190
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:22,000
I can't see the rabbit clearly.

191
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:23,440
Now I know

192
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:26,120
when I shouldn't use the flash.

193
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:26,960
When?

194
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:29,200
So should we use it in this environment?

195
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:30,620
Let's wait.

196
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:32,340
- Let's wait a little longer.
- I think we should use the flash here.

197
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:33,760
The last photo I took of you

198
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:34,560
didn't have the flash on,

199
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:35,880
so it came out yellowish.

200
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:38,400
I shouldn't point the light
directly at your face.

201
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,080
Like the lighting just now.

202
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,280
Is it a little over exposed now?

203
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:43,480
Let's see. It's fine.

204
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:44,120
Let's see.

205
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,120
We still have so many photos.

206
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,150
Let's see.

207
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:50,000
So funny.

208
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:50,720
Let's wait a little longer.

209
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,000
Let's wait.

210
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:54,320
Why is the photo so bright?

211
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:58,320
Isn't this already pretty good?

212
00:08:58,320 --> 00:09:00,080
Maybe that's just the look
it's going for.

213
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,140
(Presses)

214
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,360
Why are you pressing my face?

215
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:06,360
To make your face a little clearer.

216
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:08,960
Isn't this for...

217
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:10,560
For what? To get a good shot.

218
00:09:10,560 --> 00:09:11,960
So our photo together can...

219
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:12,680
Look a little better?

220
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:13,320
Right.

221
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,080
You'd better be.

222
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:19,300
(Tidying up)

223
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:20,740
(Notices)

224
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:24,480
You're always fixing yourself.

225
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,000
Aren't you going
to fix your hair a little?

226
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:28,560
Do I need to?

227
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:29,440
Where?

228
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:31,760
Doesn't it look fine?

229
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:32,960
I think it looks fine too.

230
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:34,740
(Notices)

231
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:37,940
(Gently strokes)

232
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:39,360
I'll try not to touch your face.

233
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:41,640
All done.

234
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:42,640
Okay.

235
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:44,200
If you touch it, you're in trouble.

236
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:45,960
What's the difference?

237
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:47,120
No difference.

238
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,840
You have a few hairs stuck to your face.

239
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:50,320
Okay.

240
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:58,880
Let me see if it's any better.

241
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:00,360
I think it's a little better.

242
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:01,800
Does it still hurt?

243
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,080
(Shows concern)

244
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:03,600
Does it itch?

245
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:04,800
It doesn't hurt if I don't touch it.

246
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:08,000
Let's put a bandage on it.

247
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:10,200
Do you want one?

248
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:11,400
Put it here?

249
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:12,680
Yeah.

250
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:20,560
Does my dress look good today?

251
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:21,400
Of course it does.

252
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:24,400
When does your dress ever not look good?

253
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,360
Of course it does.

254
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:32,720
When do your clothes ever not look good?

255
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:33,960
Okay, I get it now.

256
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:35,560
Oh, you learned it.

257
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:36,880
You taught me.

258
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:38,560
When did I teach you that?

259
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:40,800
It just came naturally.

260
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:43,280
Okay.

261
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:47,840
I was going to wear earrings today,

262
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:49,520
but this ear is inflamed.

263
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:50,760
Look.

264
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:53,120
It's really bad.

265
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,760
It's not that bad. I'm okay.

266
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,040
So I didn't wear them today.

267
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:58,760
Did you put any ointment on it?

268
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:01,120
I want it to heal in the next few days

269
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:03,880
so I can wear earrings again

270
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:06,080
when we go on a date.

271
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:12,920
Should we go upstairs?

272
00:11:12,920 --> 00:11:13,960
Let's go.

273
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,880
We can run on the treadmill together
another day.

274
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:17,640
The treadmill?

275
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:18,560
For two minutes.

276
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,040
Anything longer would wear me out.

277
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:27,080
This looks pretty good
when it's buttoned up.

278
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:27,960
When I saw it today.

279
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,360
You mean this vest?

280
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:29,600
Yeah.

281
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:30,840
I've always thought it looked good.

282
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:31,960
When I saw you today...

283
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:35,040
Do you usually wear high-collar shirts?

284
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:35,680
Not often.

285
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:36,960
But they look good on you.

286
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:38,040
Because you have a long neck.

287
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:39,400
Anyway, when I came back today

288
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:40,760
and saw you sitting there,

289
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:41,440
I thought you looked

290
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:42,840
