724
00:29:14,080 --> 00:29:15,800
Not your forearms or shoulders.

725
00:29:15,800 --> 00:29:17,440
Do you two row separately?

726
00:29:17,440 --> 00:29:19,160
Shouldn't you row in sync?

727
00:29:19,160 --> 00:29:20,840
Isn't Zhao Xilun sitting across from me?

728
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:23,040
When I row like this,
I'm driving with my back.

729
00:29:23,040 --> 00:29:23,520
And he...

730
00:29:23,520 --> 00:29:24,000
He uses his chest.

731
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:24,460
He rows like this.

732
00:29:24,460 --> 00:29:25,040
Right, using his chest.

733
00:29:25,040 --> 00:29:25,760
It's basically a chest press.

734
00:29:25,760 --> 00:29:26,760
Right.

735
00:29:26,960 --> 00:29:28,760
You two are really getting into this.

736
00:29:28,760 --> 00:29:30,440
If we had

737
00:29:30,440 --> 00:29:31,840
a rowing race,

738
00:29:31,840 --> 00:29:32,960
I don't know who'd come in first.

739
00:29:32,960 --> 00:29:34,320
It'd definitely be us.

740
00:29:34,320 --> 00:29:35,720
I know who'd come in last.

741
00:29:35,720 --> 00:29:36,880
Who?

742
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:38,720
Them.

743
00:29:38,720 --> 00:29:39,380
(Joking)

744
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:42,360
Why?

745
00:29:42,360 --> 00:29:42,960
Because...

746
00:29:42,960 --> 00:29:43,480
Cui Yihang told me

747
00:29:43,480 --> 00:29:44,600
he rowed for three hours.

748
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:48,920
That's called romance. What do you know?

749
00:29:49,640 --> 00:29:50,640
I'm kidding.

750
00:29:51,880 --> 00:29:53,080
We're training today.

751
00:29:53,080 --> 00:29:53,880
We're gonna train.

752
00:29:53,880 --> 00:29:55,200
Seriously, we're gonna win.

753
00:29:55,920 --> 00:29:57,000
Once this is over,

754
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,360
the 13 of us should

755
00:29:58,360 --> 00:29:59,640
hold our own Olympics.

756
00:29:59,640 --> 00:30:00,240
We'll do everything.

757
00:30:00,240 --> 00:30:01,800
The 800, the 1,000, swimming,

758
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:03,320
high jump, archery, horseback riding.

759
00:30:03,320 --> 00:30:05,200
You can compete on your own.

760
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:08,480
And badminton, ping-pong, tennis.

761
00:30:08,480 --> 00:30:08,880
Yeah,

762
00:30:09,120 --> 00:30:09,840
let's see who's the best.

763
00:30:13,280 --> 00:30:14,840
I saw you guys yesterday.

764
00:30:14,840 --> 00:30:15,680
We saw them.

765
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:17,840
Who was that?

766
00:30:17,840 --> 00:30:19,040
Cao Yiheng and the others.

767
00:30:19,040 --> 00:30:20,000
I think so.

768
00:30:20,200 --> 00:30:21,280
They saw us.

769
00:30:23,280 --> 00:30:24,200
Hey, guys.

770
00:30:27,240 --> 00:30:28,040
You...

771
00:30:28,700 --> 00:30:29,980
(Laughs)

772
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:31,490
Didn't we already say hi?

773
00:30:31,490 --> 00:30:31,840
Yeah.

774
00:30:31,840 --> 00:30:33,160
Weren't you guys sitting by the sofa?

775
00:30:33,640 --> 00:30:35,000
It was you guys?

776
00:30:36,440 --> 00:30:37,800
You didn't recognize us?

777
00:30:37,800 --> 00:30:39,080
He spent an hour
adjusting that telescope.

778
00:30:39,080 --> 00:30:40,560
His eyes must be...

779
00:30:40,560 --> 00:30:41,680
His eyes were all blurry.

780
00:30:42,520 --> 00:30:43,400
You're "From the Stars",

781
00:30:43,400 --> 00:30:44,600
so why can't you see any stars?

782
00:30:44,600 --> 00:30:46,360
Because he's from Baoding.

783
00:30:46,880 --> 00:30:47,680
Exactly.

784
00:30:53,200 --> 00:30:54,260
(Zhao Xilun and Sha Yue'er's
date at the stargazing room)

785
00:30:54,260 --> 00:30:54,960
Let's sit for a bit.

786
00:30:54,960 --> 00:30:55,520
Okay.

787
00:30:57,200 --> 00:30:58,280
Do you believe in fate?

788
00:30:58,880 --> 00:30:59,440
Fate?

789
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:03,320
Lately, I kind of do.

790
00:31:03,800 --> 00:31:04,600
Why?

791
00:31:05,320 --> 00:31:06,360
I just feel like

792
00:31:06,880 --> 00:31:08,240
everything happens for a reason.

793
00:31:08,240 --> 00:31:09,360
I think it's more of a mindset,

794
00:31:09,360 --> 00:31:10,340
not really believing in fate.

795
00:31:10,340 --> 00:31:11,640
(I think it's more of a mindset,
not really believing in fate)

796
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:13,160
I think some things

797
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:14,600
really are meant to happen.

798
00:31:14,600 --> 00:31:16,240
Or,

799
00:31:16,240 --> 00:31:17,960
to put it more elegantly,

800
00:31:17,960 --> 00:31:19,840
I think history
and the way things develop

801
00:31:19,840 --> 00:31:21,800
have an inevitable course.

802
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:23,640
You could

803
00:31:23,640 --> 00:31:25,400
call that fate.

804
00:31:27,400 --> 00:31:28,800
Lately, I've really felt like a lot

805
00:31:29,560 --> 00:31:31,120
of things are just coincidences.

806
00:31:34,040 --> 00:31:34,440
So many

807
00:31:34,440 --> 00:31:35,120
things

808
00:31:35,120 --> 00:31:36,160
in my life,

809
00:31:36,160 --> 00:31:37,360
the things I've wanted to do,

810
00:31:37,360 --> 00:31:38,480
are actually happening one by one.

811
00:31:38,480 --> 00:31:39,840
Would you call that fate?

812
00:31:39,840 --> 00:31:40,520
I don't think so.

813
00:31:40,520 --> 00:31:41,600
I just feel like

814
00:31:41,600 --> 00:31:43,080
if I've done everything I can,

815
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:44,120
whatever's meant to happen will happen.

816
00:31:44,120 --> 00:31:45,440
And if it doesn't, that's okay too.

817
00:31:47,720 --> 00:31:48,600
You've got

818
00:31:49,040 --> 00:31:50,320
a pretty good outlook.

819
00:31:51,880 --> 00:31:52,960
There's no point
in feeling bad about it.

820
00:31:52,960 --> 00:31:54,000
I think

821
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:56,640
I used to get too caught up thinking

822
00:31:56,640 --> 00:31:59,080
about futures
that weren't even possible.

823
00:31:59,080 --> 00:32:00,920
And those futures would usually

824
00:32:00,920 --> 00:32:02,320
require me to change things

825
00:32:02,320 --> 00:32:03,920
that already happened.

826
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:05,760
That's a contradiction in itself.

827
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:07,280
For example,

828
00:32:07,280 --> 00:32:08,320
back in college,

829
00:32:08,320 --> 00:32:09,920
my grades were pretty average,

830
00:32:09,920 --> 00:32:11,120
so I was in a bad mood all the time.

831
00:32:12,080 --> 00:32:13,000
I was pretty down.

832
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:15,720
In a bad mood? Why?

833
00:32:15,720 --> 00:32:16,840
Did something happen?

834
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:18,840
It just kind of broke

835
00:32:18,840 --> 00:32:20,360
the feedback loop

836
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:23,280
that kept me motivated to study.

837
00:32:23,960 --> 00:32:25,200
When I first got to college,

838
00:32:25,640 --> 00:32:27,320
I really had a hard time adjusting.

839
00:32:27,560 --> 00:32:29,960
It happens at first.

840
00:32:30,560 --> 00:32:32,360
Everything
about the system was different.

841
00:32:33,880 --> 00:32:35,120
Did you ever have a hard time adjusting?

842
00:32:35,120 --> 00:32:36,080
Yeah.

843
00:32:36,080 --> 00:32:37,920
How long did it last?

844
00:32:37,920 --> 00:32:39,320
Pretty much all of freshman year.

845
00:32:40,120 --> 00:32:41,520
I was in a pretty bad place.

846
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:43,920
But you gradually adjusted, right?

847
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:44,680
After all,

848
00:32:44,680 --> 00:32:46,520
you're so smart, right?

849
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:49,680
You're so smart.

850
00:32:49,680 --> 00:32:51,080
Not as smart as you.

851
00:32:51,720 --> 00:32:53,520
Not as smart as you.

852
00:32:54,840 --> 00:32:55,880
Only someone as smart

853
00:32:55,880 --> 00:32:57,800
as me could recognize how smart you are.

854
00:33:00,280 --> 00:33:02,760
You should wear a shirt,

855
00:33:02,760 --> 00:33:04,360
put on those glasses,

856
00:33:04,360 --> 00:33:05,320
and wear a tie.

857
00:33:05,320 --> 00:33:06,000
Then stand over there

858
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:06,840
doing this.

859
00:33:08,360 --> 00:33:09,240
Like this?

860
00:33:09,240 --> 00:33:10,040
Right.

861
00:33:10,600 --> 00:33:12,200
But these glasses aren't quite right.

862
00:33:12,200 --> 00:33:13,040
Don't smile.

863
00:33:13,040 --> 00:33:14,520
You have to look serious.

864
00:33:27,220 --> 00:33:29,260
(Don't go anywhere. The next episode
is even more romantic.)
